# Managed by Ansible (postgresql role). initdb's default trusts every local connection: any
# process on the box could connect as any role, the superuser included, without a password.
# Here the postgres OS user is trusted through the unix socket (peer), and everything else,
# socket or loopback, proves a password (scram-sha-256, which every role's password is hashed with).
# TYPE  DATABASE        USER            ADDRESS                 METHOD
local   all             postgres                                peer
local   all             all                                     scram-sha-256
host    all             all             127.0.0.1/32            scram-sha-256
host    all             all             ::1/128                 scram-sha-256
local   replication     postgres                                peer
host    replication     all             127.0.0.1/32            scram-sha-256
host    replication     all             ::1/128                 scram-sha-256
